{"author":{"id":"ad87ffa09351c4e5a412ec8ee1546e86b314f33d6f28629bb4bcfe7b2290924d"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794225923,"nonce":"OyL0m5w4txwV66nyyYtIYfwWqBM=","title":"Split document content from users' library entries","message":"A document is keyed by the hash of (lang, text) and has one importer, so two users importing the same text share one row. Two consequences:\n- importText (api/src/controllers/documents.ts:49) calls share() whenever the row is private and the request asks for public, without checking the requester is the importer. Another user importing the same text as public puts the first importer's document, with their title, in Explore and becomes its licensor.\n- A second importer is never recorded (mine() doesn't list it), and remove() (:117) deletes the row and doc/{id}/ blobs for everyone.\n\nModel: document_content (id hash, lang, text, blobs, status) and user_document (user, document, title, visibility, licence, author, source, imported). Deleting removes the user's entry; content goes when no entries remain. Visibility and sharing are per entry. From Gemini's review (docs/REVIEW.md 1.4).","files":null}]}